{"title":"Quantum API","sub":"Leave the cloud? Only partly.","type":"Cost & operations","industry":"Software","geo":"United States","diff":2,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Make vs buy · total cost of ownership · peak vs average load","prompt":"Quantum runs payment APIs for online shops. Its cloud bill is $14M a year and growing 25% a year with the business. The CTO proposes moving everything onto servers Quantum owns, in rented data-centre space, saying it would halve the bill. The CFO asks you to test it over the next four years.","clarify":[{"q":"What runs on the cloud?","a":"About 60% is steady traffic that runs all day. 40% is spiky: big sales days and batch jobs, sometimes 5× normal load for a few hours."},{"q":"Cost to move steady work?","a":"$12M of servers, sized for year-4 volume and lasting four years, plus $2M to migrate. Then $1.8M a year for space and power, and 8 engineers at $180k each."},{"q":"Cost to move spiky work too?","a":"Owned servers would have to be sized for year-4 peaks: another $24M of servers, $1M to migrate, $1.6M a year of space and power, 4 more engineers."},{"q":"Anything else?","a":"Ignore resale value of servers after four years."}],"structure":{"root":"Should Quantum move off the cloud, and how much of it?","branches":[{"head":"Workloads","items":["Steady vs spiky","Growth"]},{"head":"Cost of each option","items":["Cloud bill","Servers, migration","Space, power, engineers"]},{"head":"Risks","items":["Reliability","Engineering distraction","Peak capacity"]}]},"hypothesis":"Owning servers is cheap for steady load but expensive for peaks, because you pay for peak capacity all year. I expect moving only the steady part to win.","questions":[{"q":"Here is the projected cloud bill. What would it cost over four years to stay on the cloud?","exhibit":{"kind":"table","headers":["","Total bill ($M)","Steady 60%","Spiky 40%"],"rows":[["Year 1","14.0","8.4","5.6"],["Year 2","17.5","10.5","7.0"],["Year 3","21.9","13.1","8.8"],["Year 4","27.3","16.4","10.9"],["Total","80.7","48.4","32.3"]],"title":"Exhibit 1 · Cloud bill at 25% growth a year","note":null,"align":["l","r","r","r"],"boldLast":true},"answer":"<p>Four-year cloud bill: <b>$80.7M</b>.</p>"},{"q":"Compare: move only the steady work (hybrid), or move everything.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"394.471437pt\" height=\"163.444pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 394.471437 163.444\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 163.444 L 394.471437 163.444 L 394.471437 0 L 0 0 L 0 163.444 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 41.311438 138.336 L 387.271438 138.336 L 387.271438 10.824 L 41.311438 10.824 L 41.311438 138.336 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"mff7d576334\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#mff7d576334\" x=\"101.966762\" y=\"138.336\" style=\"fill: #555555; stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #555555\" transform=\"translate(73.893793 154.03) scale(0.09 -0.09)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-2e\" d=\"M 3187 3866 Q 3021 4064 2758 4205 Q 2496 4346 2099 4346 Q 1619 4346 1344 4134 Q 1069 3923 1069 3546 Q 1069 3443 1117 3308 Q 1165 3174 1312 3046 Q 1459 2918 1754 2816 L 2682 2509 Q 3264 2317 3507 2000 Q 3750 1683 3750 1254 Q 3750 845 3545 547 Q 3341 250 2963 93 Q 2586 -64 2054 -64 Q 1670 -64 1344 29 Q 1018 122 765 298 Q 512 474 333 736 Q 301 781 310 816 Q 320 851 371 890 L 602 1050 Q 666 1088 701 1088 Q 736 1088 762 1050 Q 934 832 1100 688 Q 1267 544 1488 473 Q 1709 403 2029 403 Q 2534 403 2848 585 Q 3162 768 3162 1190 Q 3162 1350 3098 1481 Q 3034 1613 2880 1725 Q 2726 1837 2438 1946 L 1466 2278 Q 1114