2 4717 764 4733 Q 787 4749 877 4749 L 3482 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" d=\"M 1869 -58 Q 1626 -58 1424 -6 Q 1222 45 1062 134 Q 902 224 784 336 Q 666 448 582 563 Q 570 589 566 617 Q 563 646 602 666 L 966 813 Q 998 832 1020 816 Q 1043 800 1062 774 Q 1197 608 1389 505 Q 1581 403 1869 403 Q 2323 403 2611 627 Q 2899 851 3036 1238 Q 3174 1626 3174 2112 Q 3174 2221 3158 2249 Q 3142 2278 3066 2240 Q 2822 2118 2550 2016 Q 2278 1914 1894 1914 Q 1414 1914 1065 2096 Q 717 2278 534 2592 Q 352 2906 352 3302 Q 352 3757 569 4096 Q 787 4435 1164 4620 Q 1542 4806 2003 4806 Q 2554 4806 2954 4528 Q 3354 4250 3571 3722 Q 3789 3194 3789 2445 Q 3789 1664 3555 1104 Q 3322 544 2896 243 Q 2470 -58 1869 -58 L 1869 -58 z\nM 1965 2362 Q 2150 2362 2348 2403 Q 2547 2445 2732 2521 Q 2918 2598 3046 2688 Q 3123 2739 3148 2793 Q 3174 2848 3174 2963 Q 3174 3187 3104 3430 Q 3034 3674 2890 3885 Q 2746 4096 2525 4227 Q 2304 4358 2003 4358 Q 1709 4358 1472 4224 Q 1235 4090 1097 3856 Q 960 3622 960 3328 Q 960 3059 1085 2838 Q 1210 2618 1434 2490 Q 1658 2362 1965 2362 L 1965 2362 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-89\" transform=\"translate(65.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(131.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(152.109375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_12\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(318.879863 44.272238) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" d=\"M 2637 486 Q 2707 486 2707 422 L 2707 64 Q 2707 45 2691 22 Q 2675 0 2637 0 L 390 0 Q 320 0 320 64 L 320 422 Q 320 486 390 486 L 1197 486 Q 1248 486 1248 518 L 1248 4038 Q 1248 4102 1190 4090 L 397 3795 Q 314 3776 314 3872 L 314 4128 Q 314 4173 326 4189 Q 339 4205 378 4224 L 1325 4698 Q 1389 4730 1427 4739 Q 1466 4749 1517 4749 L 1792 4749 Q 1862 4749 1862 4672 L 1862 531 Q 1862 486 1901 486 L 2637 486 L 2637 486 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-86\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(66.09375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(112.59375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(133.5 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pcb78fbf790\"><rect x=\"41.311438\" y=\"10.824\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 2 · Four-year cost ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p><b>Hybrid:</b> servers $12M + migration $2M + running $3.24M × 4 = $27.0M, plus the spiky cloud bill $32.3M = <b>$59.2M</b>. Saving: <b>$21.5M</b>.</p> <p><b>Everything:</b> hybrid's own costs plus $24M + $1M + $2.32M × 4 for the spiky part = <b>$61.2M</b>. Saving: $19.5M.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> moving the spiky work costs $34.3M against $32.3M of cloud bill: it loses money. The cloud is cheapest exactly where load is uneven.</p>"},{"q":"The CTO says the full move 'halves the bill'. Where does that come from, and what is it missing?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>It probably compares the yearly running cost of owned servers with the cloud bill, ignoring the upfront servers, migration and, most of all, the extra capacity needed for peaks. Other risks: reliability (Quantum now runs its own hardware), hiring 12 specialist engineers, and the team's attention moving away from the product.</p>"}],"reco":"Move only the steady 60% of workloads onto owned servers and keep the spiky work on the cloud. Over four years that costs about $59.2M against $80.7M for staying on the cloud, saving about $21.5M. Moving everything saves less ($19.5M), because servers sized for rare peaks sit idle most of the time. Risk: reliability and hiring, so migrate in stages with a fallback to the cloud. Next step: confirm how steady the 60% really is with three months of usage data.","great":["Splits steady from spiky load","Includes upfront, migration and running costs over the full period","Spots that peak capacity makes owning expensive","Challenges the 'halves the bill' claim with numbers"],"id":52,"slug":"quantum-api"}